```javascript
class FraudDetector {
  constructor() {
    this.transactions = []; // Stores all transactions
    this.flaggedTransactions = new Set();
    this.blacklistedUsers = new Set();
    this.userTransactionHistory = new Map(); // Maps userId -> List of transactions
  }

  addTransaction({ id, userId, amount, timestamp, country, device }) {
    if (!this.userTransactionHistory.has(userId)) {
      this.userTransactionHistory.set(userId, []);
    }

    const userTransactions = this.userTransactionHistory.get(userId);

    // Store transaction
    this.transactions.push({ id, userId, amount, timestamp, country, device });
    userTransactions.push({ id, amount, timestamp, country, device });

    // Check for fraud
    this.checkVelocity(userId);
    this.checkAnomalousSpending(userId);

    // These checks still need to be implemented
    // this.checkGeolocation(userId);
    // this.checkDeviceFingerprinting(userId);

    // Blacklist user if they have 3 or more flagged transactions
    if (this.getFlaggedCount(userId) >= 3) {
      this.blacklistedUsers.add(userId);
    }
  }

  checkVelocity(userId) {
    const userTransactions = this.userTransactionHistory.get(userId);
    const latestTx = userTransactions[userTransactions.length - 1];

    // Check last 5 transactions
    if (userTransactions.length >= 5) {
      const firstTxInWindow = userTransactions[userTransactions.length - 5];
      if (latestTx.timestamp - firstTxInWindow.timestamp <= 60000) {
        this.flaggedTransactions.add(latestTx.id);
      }
    }
  }

  checkAnomalousSpending(userId) {
    const userTransactions = this.userTransactionHistory.get(userId);
    if (userTransactions.length < 10) return; // Need enough data

    const latestTx = userTransactions[userTransactions.length - 1];
    const last10 = userTransactions.slice(-10);
    const avg = last10.reduce((sum, tx) => sum + tx.amount, 0) / 10;

    if (latestTx.amount > avg * 10) {
      this.flaggedTransactions.add(latestTx.id);
    }
  }

  getFlaggedCount(userId) {
    return [...this.flaggedTransactions].filter((id) =>
      this.userTransactionHistory.get(userId).some((tx) => tx.id === id)
    ).length;
  }
}

module.exports = { FraudDetector };
```


Prompt:
I am building a fraud detection system in JavaScript that analyzes user transactions and flags suspicious activities based on multiple fraud detection rules. My system should identify patterns indicating fraudulent behavior and blacklist users who exceed a threshold of flagged transactions. Right now, I have a basic fraud detection system that can process transactions and apply some fraud detection rules. However, I want to enhance it by implementing additional fraud detection methods and making it more robust.

These are the enhancements I need you to work on:

1. Velocity Check (Already Implemented, Needs Optimization)
- If a user makes 5 or more transactions within 60 seconds, flag the latest transaction.

2. Anomalous Spending Check (Partially Implemented, Needs Improvement)
- If a transaction amount is 10× higher than the user’s average of their last 10 transactions, flag it.

3. Geolocation Fraud Check (New, Needs Implementation)
- If a user’s transactions occur from two different countries within 5 minutes, flag them.

4. Device Fingerprinting Check (New, Needs Implementation)
- If a user makes two transactions from different devices within 10 minutes, flag them.

5. Blacklisting Users (Partially Implemented, Needs Finalization)
- If a user has 3 or more flagged transactions, they should be blacklisted.

